# One file per company: copy this to e.g. companies/acme.env (keep company files out of the repository)
# and run:  deploy/new-company.sh companies/acme.env
# No secrets here. The database address and the SMTP password are asked for when the script runs,
# or read from the environment variables MONGODB_URI and SMTP_PASS. The JWT secret is generated.
# The file is read by bash: put a value with spaces or < > in double quotes.

# --- Required ---
# The Google Cloud project the company's copy lives in, and its region.
PROJECT_ID=marichi-fleet
# Default: Johannesburg, the region closest to Zambia. Cloud Run domain mappings are not offered there,
# so a custom domain goes through a load balancer (DOMAIN_MODE=lb).
REGION=africa-south1
# Short name: 3–30 lowercase letters, digits or hyphens. Used in every resource name.
COMPANY=acme-transport
# The company's first Owner. On first start the account is created and e-mailed a link to choose a password.
OWNER_EMAIL=owner@acme-transport.example
# Outgoing e-mail, required in production for invitations and password resets.
SMTP_HOST=smtp.mandrillapp.com
SMTP_FROM="Acme Fleet <no-reply@acme-transport.example>"

# --- Optional (defaults shown) ---
# SMTP_PORT=587
# SMTP_SECURE=false
# SMTP_USER=

# The public address. Empty: the Cloud Run address (https://fleet-<company>-<number>.<region>.run.app).
# DOMAIN=fleet.acme-transport.example
# How the domain is served:
#   lb       an external HTTPS load balancer with a Google-managed certificate (any region; about US$18 a month)
#   mapping  a Cloud Run domain mapping (free, but only in some regions, not africa-south1)
#   none     no custom domain
# DOMAIN_MODE=lb

# How the service reaches the database:
#   static   through Cloud NAT with one reserved address, so the Atlas access list holds that single address
#   open     Google's shared addresses; the Atlas access list must then allow 0.0.0.0/0
# EGRESS=static
# NETWORK=default
# SUBNET=default

# Instances. More than one needs REDIS_URL (Memorystore), so sign-in rate limits are shared.
# MIN_INSTANCES=0
# MAX_INSTANCES=1
# REDIS_URL=
# CPU=1
# MEMORY=512Mi

# Where the images are (built with deploy/build-image.sh and shared by every company). The version to
# run is given to new-company.sh and update-company.sh, never kept here.
# IMAGE_REPO=africa-south1-docker.pkg.dev/marichi-fleet/fleet/fleet-erp

# The API test console at /console/ (off in production unless needed).
# CONSOLE_ENABLED=false
# UPLOAD_MAX_MB=15

# Resource names, derived from COMPANY unless set:
# SERVICE=fleet-acme-transport
# SERVICE_ACCOUNT=fleet-acme-transport
# BUCKET=marichi-fleet-acme-transport-files
